 **Before writing anything**: read `{{DOC_PRINCIPLES_ARTICLE}}` in full — the Core doc principles section there is the single source of truth for destination rules, diagram-first ordering, coloring tokens, format priority, the certainty principle, coverage-keys-over-headings, and length budgets. Apply it as written; nothing here duplicates it. Also read `{{DOC_STRUCTURE_ARTICLE}}` for tier placement and naming conventions, and the applicable Intent article for the document's required semantic coverage.
 
+**Terminology**: read `{{TERMINOLOGY_REGISTRY}}`. When the content you're writing names a project concept already in the registry, use its approved form — never a forbidden synonym, even if the input material used one. When the content coins a project-specific term that recurs and isn't registered yet, append a row (`Term`, `Approved form`, `Forbidden synonyms`, `Definition`, `Introduced in` — the current doc's path) before finishing to write. Skip standard English, well-known industry terms, and one-off words — the registry is for project-specific concepts at risk of drifting, not a full glossary.
